{"name":"Disruption with some GitHub services","status":"resolved","created_at":"2026-01-22T14:12:49.865Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T20:27:38.867Z","monitoring_at":null,"resolved_at":"2026-01-22T15:22:59.780Z","impact":"minor","shortlink":"https://stspg.io/1vqlgvn4h35h","scheduled_for":null,"scheduled_until":null,"scheduled_remind_prior":false,"scheduled_reminded_at":null,"impact_override":"minor","scheduled_auto_in_progress":false,"scheduled_auto_completed":false,"metadata":{},"started_at":"2026-01-22T14:12:49.856Z","reminder_intervals":null,"id":"cqb5hcy0gx18","page_id":"kctbh9vrtdwd","incident_updates":[{"status":"resolved","body":"On January 22, 2026, our authentication service experienced an issue between 14:00 UTC and 14:50 UTC, resulting in downstream disruptions for users.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eFrom 14:00 UTC to 14:23 UTC, authenticated API requests experienced higher-than-normal error rates, with an average of 16.9% and occasional peaks up to 22.2% resulting in HTTP 401 responses for authenticated API requests. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eFrom 14:00 UTC to 14:50 UTC, git operations over HTTP were impacted, with error rates averaging 3.8% and peaking at 10.8%. As a result, some users may have been unable to run git commands as expected.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis was due to the authentication service reaching the maximum allowed number of database connections. We mitigated the incident by increasing the maximum number of database connections in the authentication service.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWe are adding additional monitoring around database connection pool usage and improving our traffic projection to reduce our time to detection and mitigation of issues like this one in the future.\u003cbr /\u003e","created_at":"2026-01-22T15:22:59.780Z","wants_twitter_update":false,"twitter_updated_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-01-27T20:27:38.862Z","display_at":"2026-01-22T15:22:59.780Z","deliver_notifications":true,"tweet_id":null,"id":"87q80cqdx7fg","incident_id":"cqb5hcy0gx18","custom_tweet":null,"affected_components":[{"code":"kr09ddfgbfsf","name":"Issues","old_status":"operational","new_status":"operational"}]},{"status":"investigating","body":"We have identified an issue in one of our services and have mitigated it. Services have recovered and we have a mitigation but we are working on a longer term solution.","created_at":"2026-01-22T15:22:31.283Z","wants_twitter_update":false,"twitter_updated_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-01-22T15:22:31.283Z","display_at":"2026-01-22T15:22:31.283Z","deliver_notifications":true,"tweet_id":null,"id":"grhyt4zkdkbm","incident_id":"cqb5hcy0gx18","custom_tweet":null,"affected_components":[{"code":"kr09ddfgbfsf","name":"Issues","old_status":"operational","new_status":"operational"}]},{"status":"investigating","body":"Issues is operating normally.","created_at":"2026-01-22T14:27:54.270Z","wants_twitter_update":false,"twitter_updated_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-01-22T14:27:54.270Z","display_at":"2026-01-22T14:27:54.270Z","deliver_notifications":true,"tweet_id":null,"id":"by8k8qfw7hgb","incident_id":"cqb5hcy0gx18","custom_tweet":null,"affected_components":[{"code":"kr09ddfgbfsf","name":"Issues","old_status":"partial_outage","new_status":"operational"}]},{"status":"investigating","body":"Issues is experiencing degraded performance. We are continuing to investigate.","created_at":"2026-01-22T14:23:44.549Z","wants_twitter_update":false,"twitter_updated_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-01-22T14:23:44.549Z","display_at":"2026-01-22T14:23:44.549Z","deliver_notifications":true,"tweet_id":null,"id":"5zz1s96dyhhx","incident_id":"cqb5hcy0gx18","custom_tweet":null,"affected_components":[{"code":"kr09ddfgbfsf","name":"Issues","old_status":"operational","new_status":"partial_outage"}]},{"status":"investigating","body":"We are investigating reports of impacted performance for some GitHub services.","created_at":"2026-01-22T14:12:49.910Z","wants_twitter_update":false,"twitter_updated_at":null